This product includes software developed within the COPSE project and has
been modified for the study of a temperature-dependent, substrate-limited
reverse-weathering feedback on the deep-time carbon-silica cycle.

Modified files
--------------
- COPSE_frontend.m : parameter blocks, initial conditions and switches for
                     the marine silica cycle, the alkalinity-DIC closure and
                     the calibration runs.
- COPSE_equations.m: state vector expanded from 24 to 27 by adding DSi (25),
                     alkalinity (26) and DIC (27); new flux terms for reverse
                     weathering, biogenic and abiotic silica burial,
                     carbonate burial and air-sea CO2 exchange.
- readme.md        : section "Modifications for this study (2026)".

